WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
Rosa compares three ways an annuity can develop value.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.580
One credits interest declared by the insurer.

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.680
Another uses selected investment portfolios.

4
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.220
A third calculates interest using a market index and a contract

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:20.340
formula. The key question is who bears the investment risk and

6
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.760
exactly what is guaranteed.

7
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.840
Income timing is a different classification: fixed, indexed or

8
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.000
variable describes the design, while immediate or deferred describes

9
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.960
when income starts. An early withdrawal can also produce a market

10
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.440
value adjustment under some contracts.

11
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.540
Keep the source of growth, minimum promise, withdrawal rules and

12
00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.820
selected income benefit separate when comparing these choices.

13
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:55.373
A traditional fixed annuity is supported by the insurer's general account.

14
00:00:56.193 --> 00:00:59.833
The insurer bears the investment risk behind its contractual guarantees.

15
00:01:00.813 --> 00:01:05.453
Suppose Rosa's contract guarantees at least two percent interest but

16
00:01:05.453 --> 00:01:08.433
currently credits four percent for the stated period.

17
00:01:09.253 --> 00:01:12.233
Four percent is not automatically promised forever.

18
00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:17.113
A later declared rate can change within the contract's limits while

19
00:01:17.113 --> 00:01:19.173
the minimum guarantee remains applicable.

20
00:01:19.893 --> 00:01:24.593
Some designs guarantee a stated rate for several years; read that

21
00:01:24.593 --> 00:01:29.653
period. A fixed income option can provide level dollar payments, but

22
00:01:29.653 --> 00:01:32.993
level dollars do not guarantee level purchasing power.

23
00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.773
Inflation can reduce what the same monthly amount buys.

24
00:01:37.657 --> 00:01:39.557
David considers a variable annuity.

25
00:01:40.077 --> 00:01:43.197
Amounts allocated to its investment subaccounts are held in a separate

26
00:01:43.197 --> 00:01:46.057
account, with results tied to the chosen portfolios.

27
00:01:47.097 --> 00:01:50.417
He bears the investment risk for that allocation, and value can

28
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:53.937
fall. In a simplified example with no charges or other changes,

29
00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:57.590
fifty thousand dollars experiencing a ten percent loss becomes forty-five

30
00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:01.997
thousand dollars. Actual fees and withdrawals also affect value.

31
00:02:02.537 --> 00:02:05.897
Variable income payments can change with investment results under the payout

32
00:02:05.897 --> 00:02:09.697
formula. A guarantee applies only to the benefit and conditions it

33
00:02:09.697 --> 00:02:13.657
names. Read its limits instead of assuming all account values are

34
00:02:13.657 --> 00:02:17.817
protected. Variable annuities are securities as well as insurance products,

35
00:02:18.357 --> 00:02:21.137
with prospectus disclosures and applicable securities requirements.

36
00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:26.413
A fixed indexed annuity uses a specified index to calculate interest

37
00:02:26.413 --> 00:02:30.313
under the contract. It does not give Rosa direct ownership of

38
00:02:30.313 --> 00:02:33.793
that index's stocks. Suppose the stated method uses an eight percent

39
00:02:33.793 --> 00:02:37.373
index increase, a fifty percent participation rate and a three percent

40
00:02:37.373 --> 00:02:39.693
cap, with no spread or other adjustment.

41
00:02:40.353 --> 00:02:42.813
Half of eight percent is four percent, then the cap limits

42
00:02:42.813 --> 00:02:44.573
the credited rate to three percent.

43
00:02:44.573 --> 00:02:46.613
Apply the provided order and formula.

44
00:02:46.613 --> 00:02:50.793
A zero index-credit floor prevents a negative index credit under that

45
00:02:50.793 --> 00:02:54.953
provision; it does not eliminate surrender charges, rider costs or other

46
00:02:54.953 --> 00:02:58.813
reductions. Registered index-linked annuities are different and can expose

47
00:02:58.813 --> 00:03:00.153
value to index losses.

48
00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:05.848
A market-value-adjusted annuity may guarantee interest for a specified period

49
00:03:05.848 --> 00:03:08.948
while adjusting value if the owner exits at a time covered

50
00:03:08.948 --> 00:03:13.528
by its formula. Such designs are also associated with the term

51
00:03:13.528 --> 00:03:18.408
modified guaranteed annuity. Generally, an increase in relevant market

52
00:03:18.408 --> 00:03:22.548
interest rates can produce a negative adjustment; a decrease can produce

53
00:03:22.548 --> 00:03:26.248
a positive adjustment. The actual formula and timing control.

54
00:03:26.248 --> 00:03:30.628
A market value adjustment is distinct from a surrender charge, and

55
00:03:30.628 --> 00:03:34.528
both may apply. Do not assume keeping the credited interest guarantee

56
00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:37.488
means every early withdrawal returns the same amount.

57
00:03:38.328 --> 00:03:41.388
Registered market-value-adjustment annuities also have securities

58
00:03:41.388 --> 00:03:45.508
disclosures; the presence of an adjustment alone does not replace a

59
00:03:45.508 --> 00:03:50.345
product's actual classification. Rosa wants predictable promises

60
00:03:50.825 --> 00:03:53.665
and David is willing to accept investment fluctuations.

61
00:03:54.645 --> 00:03:58.565
Their preferences begin the discussion, but neither preference alone

62
00:03:58.565 --> 00:04:00.725
establishes the right recommendation.

63
00:04:01.845 --> 00:04:06.925
Compare costs, accessible cash, the time horizon, the

64
00:04:06.925 --> 00:04:11.145
insurer, the actual guarantees and the income option.

65
00:04:11.585 --> 00:04:14.865
A high illustrated return is not a guaranteed result.

66
00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:20.645
An indexed design is not automatically a variable annuity, and a

67
00:04:20.645 --> 00:04:24.365
separate account is not the same as the insurer's general account.

68
00:04:24.985 --> 00:04:28.105
For an exam, identify the design from its mechanics.

69
00:04:29.105 --> 00:04:32.645
Then answer the particular question about value, credited interest,

70
00:04:33.225 --> 00:04:34.965
investment risk or surrender.

71
00:04:35.985 --> 00:04:40.425
A product label cannot override the numbers and conditions explicitly given.
